@andy-armstrong If we allow renaming random cohorts, we have to update the cohort_config advanced setting. Otherwise, this is what happens-- the renamed random cohort converts into a manual cohort (keeping the students previously in the random cohort), and a new random cohort is created with the original name. This is because the random cohorts are stored by name, not by ID.

I'm really leaning towards not allowing renaming of cohorts with this work. I don't think it would be confusing if the name doesn't appear in the settings tab-- I don't think the user would necessarily expect the "new cohort" form to be identical to the "settings tab". The code could stay as-is, just hide the cohort name field for settings.

